infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Mutex or channel — the qualified slogan
  desc Both mint the same happens-before edges; pick the one that makes ownership obvious
  compares
    - label Mutex: protect state in place
      children
        - label Counter or in-place cache
          desc Shared state mutated where it lives
        - label Multi-field invariant
          desc Two fields that must change together
        - label Lock-mutate-unlock methods
          desc A struct guarding its own fields
        - label Tiny critical section
          desc Never hold across I/O or a channel op
    - label Channel: transfer ownership
      children
        - label Pipeline stage handoff
          desc Pass work items to the next stage
        - label Worker pool
          desc Distribute jobs across goroutines
        - label Cancellation / lifecycle
          desc close signals done to many waiters
        - label Exclusive buffer ownership
          desc Exactly one goroutine may touch it now
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6
